22 0 obj
<< /A 496 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows an axial MRI scan of the pelvis with a large, well-defined mass \(mucinous cystadenoma\) in the central region highlighted in teal, while panel B shows a similar scan with the mass \(serous cystadenocarcinoma\) highlighted in red.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 15 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 497 0 R /Alt (Flowchart diagram showing data processing for ovarian tumor classification, starting with four tumor types and case numbers, filtering through MRI and DICOM images, categorizing into benign and malignant ovarian tumors, followed by manual segmentation, radiomics feature extraction, 80-20 train-test split, feature selection, data scaling, classifier selection, and concluding with model construction and evaluation.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 16 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 498 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a LASSO coefficient trace plot with colored lines for different features as log\(alpha\) increases. Panel B displays a horizontal bar chart ranking feature coefficients by importance. Panel C compares calibration curves for training and test sets, contrasting predicted and actual probabilities. Panel D contains decision curve analyses for training and test datasets, plotting net benefit against threshold probability. Panel E presents ROC curves for training and test sets, illustrating true versus false positive rates for the classification model.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 17 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
